Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-r6x9-5r99-36j7: Various packet overreads in mysqlnd
 wireprotocol

Co-authored-by: Nora Dossche <7771979+ndossche@users.noreply.github.com>

Backport of php-src 114dbb74368e6a6cd6e48ddb4a76dbe8728b84e2 (PHP-8.2) to PHP 7.2:
- greeting auth_protocol: includes the NUL-bounded copy of php-src d37a20c4a2 (PHP-8.2, "Fix MySQLnd possible buffer over read in auth_protocol"), needed because the buffer NUL-termination it relied on is removed
- greeting: no MariaDB "5.5.5-" prefix handling in 7.2, so that hunk does not apply
- rset field metadata: the READ_RSET_FIELD bound check is applied to the 7.2 rset_field_offsets loop, and the 7.2 per-field BAIL checks of the fixed 12-byte block become one BAIL_IF_NOT_ENOUGH_DATA_EX(12) after the length byte warning (as in 8.2)
- caching_sha2_password does not exist in 7.2: the cached_sha2 hunk and its 4 tests are not applicable
- mysqlnd_stmt_prepare_read_eof: execute_cmd_buffer freed with mnd_pefree(.., stmt->persistent) (7.2 allocation)
- bool/true/false -> zend_bool/1/0, premature_end messages adapted from the 7.2 MYSQLND_SZ_T_SPEC variants
- not included: php-src 9e5cf96095 and 9c74d7d1bc (PHP-8.4), reverted by e318023a6b in favour of this fix
- tests: fake_server.inc additions without PHP 8 syntax, fixed port 33305 instead of the later ephemeral port helper, --SKIPIF-- instead of --EXTENSIONS--, 7.2 warning/return-value output instead of mysqli exceptions

7.1: same greeting packet parsing without the server_caps debug line.

7.0 adaptation: 7.0's mysqlnd predates the const / MYSQLND_PFC rework, so every hunk of the wire-protocol reader was re-applied by hand on top of the older code. The fix is the same:
- php_mysqlnd_net_field_length() takes the remaining packet size and returns MYSQLND_INVALID_NET_FIELD_LENGTH, php_mysqlnd_net_field_length_ll() returns MYSQLND_OPTIONAL_UINT64_T (both keep 7.0's non-const zend_uchar ** argument)
- BAIL_IF_NO_MORE_DATA (checked after the read) is replaced by BAIL_IF_NOT_ENOUGH_DATA[_EX] / BAIL_PREMATURE_END (checked before), in greet, auth response, OK, EOF, result set header, result set field, prepare, change user and sha256 public key readers
- the greeting server version, the auth plugin names (auth response and change user) are read through memchr() instead of strdup() on a possibly unterminated buffer; the greet packet no longer NUL-terminates the receive buffer
- ps_fetch_time/date/datetime check the declared length against the fixed offsets they read (ps_fetch_is_length_too_short(), zend_uchar ** here as well)
- ext/mysqli/tests/fake_server.inc and the new tests: \": void\" return types dropped, PHP 7.0 has no void return type
